## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical use of PIM, approvals, MFA, and auditing in real admin flows.

## Key Concepts

- Privileged Identity Management
- Just-In-Time access
- MFA and approvals
- Activation duration and auto-revoke
- Auditing and alerts

## Code Example

```javascript
// PIM-like REST flow (illustrative)
async function activatePIM() {
  const token = await getGraphToken(['PrivilegedIdentityManagement.Read.All']);
  const res = await fetch('https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/privilegedRoleAssignments', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      roleDefinitionId: '<role-id>',
      scope: '<scope>',
      duration: 'PT1H',
      activationApprover: '<manager@contoso.com>'
    })
  });
  return res.json();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle emergency access without cascading approvals?
- What CA or BA policies would guard this flow during off-hours?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a beginner's grasp of Conditional Access basics and practical gating for real-world apps.

## Key Concepts
- Conditional Access
- Location and device-based access
- Intune device compliance
- Sandbox validation and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Illustrative CA policy snippet (formatting for clarity)
{
  "applications": {"include": ["https://contoso-app" ]},
  "conditions": {
    "locations": {"include": ["trusted"]},
    "devices": {"include": ["compliant"]},
    "users": {"include": ["AllUsers"]}
  },
  "grant": {"operator": "OR", "builtInControls": ["mfa"]}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this policy using a sandbox user and what logs would you inspect?
- What are common pitfalls when combining location-based and device-based CA policies?
